[2026-11-25] rc:4692637894 inline on src/netbase.cpp by vasild (member) (edited 2026-11-25):
Hmm, the code in `Sock::WaitMany()` ignored `ErrorEvent` in requested events and internally would ask `select(2)` to check for error events if the caller is interested in `RecvEvent`.

This PR adds a new flag to tell `WaitMany()` that it needs to set `ErrorEvent`. Why not just pass `ErrorEvent` and stop ignoring it? No caller is passing `ErrorEvent`, so the un-ignoring will be a no-op. Then change the `ConnectToSocket()` function to use `ErrorEvent`, it will be the only caller.

Tuu many words, diff better:

